KINDNESS TAXONOMY v1.0.0 — 7 October 2026

Run from ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop after verifying the delivered ZIP SHA256.

Full local run:
  ./RUN_TAXONOMY.command --workers 10 --memory-gb 10

Cheap diagnostics first, then stop:
  ./RUN_TAXONOMY.command --workers 10 --memory-gb 10 --stop-after-diagnostics

To continue, run the full command. The same configuration reuses completed
stages. There are no percentage-checkpoint approval prompts. An interrupted
mixture reuses completed starts and bootstrap replications. The currently
unfinished fit is repeated. Avoid running two copies of the same job.

Defaults:
  Project: /Volumes/XT_Pro/lichess_kindness
  Reports: ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop
  Cache: derived/replication/kindness_taxonomy_v100_PRIVATE/<run key>

Override paths with --project-root and --desktop. Environment variables
KTX_PROJECT_ROOT, KTX_DESKTOP_DIR and KTX_PYTHON can select launcher defaults.
The data drive must be mounted. Keep the Terminal open; caffeinate prevents
idle sleep while the process runs. Closing the Mac lid can still suspend it.

What this run does
- Authenticates the existing certified 24-month pool/nonadjacent choice panel.
- Excludes __PRIVATE_VALUE_1__ and __PRIVATE_VALUE_2__ in both roles, including panel histories.
- Runs E diagnostics and relative July event-study tables first.
- Runs first-observed-grant hazard and authenticated receipt-IV history splits.
- Fits B1 account mixtures K=1..6, M=20/50/4, with 20 starts, independent
  Year-2 fits, held-out validation, and 200 main-model account bootstraps.
- Fits B2 type-specific state/cost logits at B1-selected K, with common
  stage/speed/month controls and 200 main-model account bootstraps.
- Produces account-type/posterior/marker Parquet files locally, aggregate
  tables, figures, and source/schema inventory in the return ZIP.
- Runs the D1/D2/F estimators if separately authenticated extended inputs exist.

What requires the next data build
All-game resignation/disconnection/casual/activity/rating markers; ordinary
continuation-game trajectories and random-sample engine calibration; full-game
accuracy; and evaluated outoftime events for probable waiting. The current
choice panel does not contain their denominators. EXTENDED_INPUTS.md explains
the contracts. Missing inputs receive BLOCKED_INPUT/NEEDS_INPUT_BUILD statuses.
COMPLETE_LOCAL does not mean every item in the research plan is complete.

Runtime and memory
The diagnostics are substantially cheaper than the mixture/bootstrap jobs.
There is no production-calibrated ETA: allow hours, potentially longer, for
the full fits and 200-replication bootstraps. The 10-GB argument is a resource
budget, not a hard process-RSS cap; DuckDB is given at most 3.5 GB at the
10-GB setting, leaving room for numerical arrays. NumPy/optimizer memory and
macOS overhead are separate. Starts run sequentially to avoid 10 simultaneous
copies of the opportunity arrays. DuckDB uses up to 10 workers and BLAS 2.
Disk must accommodate a projected panel, prior-event histories, risk rows,
private type assignments, and spill files. The certified source panel is
never overwritten. The run prints 30-second heartbeats for long stages.

Outputs
KINDNESS_TAXONOMY_REPORT_<key>.zip and .zip.sha256 are refreshed after every
finished stage. A failure also produces a partial return ZIP when possible.
Start with READ_RESULTS.txt, ANALYSIS_COVERAGE.csv and summary.json. Upload
that report ZIP for interpretation or a schema-specific extension. Individual
player rows, usernames, raw game IDs and posteriors stay in PRIVATE files on
your drive; they are omitted from the return ZIP.

Integrity and reproducibility
Source checks are intentionally strict. Do not delete a failed check or relax
a sample predicate to get a run through. Return the report ZIP/log instead.
The package checksum fixes thresholds before this run. This is exploratory
work: earlier related construal and receipt results have already been seen.
It is not a retrospective preregistration. Year 2 never enters Year-1 type
assignment, but previously inspected Year-2 material is not a virgin holdout.

The launcher reuses compatible installed Python packages or creates an
isolated environment. Package installation may use the internet once; the
analysis itself blocks network calls and makes no API or Stockfish requests.
Sixteen synthetic numerical/integration tests run automatically before data
access. Validation details are in VALIDATION.txt.
